# CE Points — UI

## Theme & surfaces

- Use `ThemeColors` tokens; don’t hardcode one-off grays.
- Light and dark should **read the same structure** (e.g. chart total + overview insets via `surfaceInset` + hairline border — not white-on-white in light).
- Brand accent: track orange `#D35400` / `TRACK_COLOR`. Avoid purple/glow/AI-default aesthetics.

## Calculators

- Placeholders = world-record hints → use `colors.placeholder` (more faded than muted text).
- Typed performance values should read clearly (slightly bolder than placeholders).
- Save Score modal: clear of keyboard, not stuck to it, not shoved to the top edge.
- Prefer shared calculator components over per-event one-offs when behavior matches.

## Motion & interaction

- Prefer springs / Reanimated over linear fades for meaningful transitions.
- Motion serves hierarchy and feedback (reorder, press, open/close) — not decoration.
- Match existing patterns (FLIP reorder, edge auto-scroll, flush-before-chart) before inventing new ones.
- Haptics only where they clarify an action; don’t spam.

## Anti-patterns

- Extra cards, pill clusters, stat strips, or “marketing” chrome inside the app.
- Light-mode-only or dark-mode-only fixes that break the other theme.
- Large refactors when a token or spacing tweak would do.
